<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jerusalem (And did those feet in ancient time)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">poem in the preface to Milton, title page dated <a href="/years/1804">1804</a>, printed c. 1808; music written 10 March <a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as And did those feet in ancient time</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The words are a short poem by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-blake">William Blake</a> in the preface to his epic Milton: A Poem in Two Books. The title page bears the date 1804, probably when Blake began the plates, but the poem was printed around 1808. Blake wrote much of Milton while living in a cottage at Felpham in Sussex; local tradition at Lavant, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a>, holds instead that he wrote this poem in a public house there.</p></div>
